       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Confirming the dose doesn't change the safety problem. 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg/day. I can't find a clinical indication for it, and you haven't given a rationale. I also can't verify any approvals from my side.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Dose within the labeled range:** Give me the dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Dose above the labeled range:** If a specialist, such as psychiatry or toxicology, has recommended it, please get pharmacy or the prescriber to review and enter it. They can document the rationale and set up monitoring, such as ECG and serotonin toxicity checks.\n- **Possible overdose or ingestion:** If this is about an overdose, this isn't a standing order. Contact poison control or toxicology urgently.\n\nI'm glad to help with any of these."
